Account Service does not directly join or map the Customer entity. It stores only customerId and uses the Customer Service API to validate the customer. This preserves the microservice boundary.

3. Account → Customer REST Communication

Configuration

services.customer.base-url=${CUSTOMER_SERVICE_URL:http://localhost:8080}

The base URL is externalized so local development can use localhost while later environments can provide a different service address without changing source code.

CustomerClient responsibilities

Call Customer Service using Spring RestClient.

Return the minimal customer information required by Account Service.

Treat HTTP 404 as an invalid/nonexistent customer.

Convert downstream 5xx and connection failures into CustomerServiceUnavailableException.

Avoid importing Customer Service DTO classes into Account Service.

4. Account Creation Validation

Before creating an account, Account Service now verifies:

The customer exists.

The customer is ACTIVE.

The customer does not already have the requested account type.

The downstream Customer Service is available.

Only after these checks succeed does Account Service save the account and allow Oracle to generate the business account number.


