8. Automated Unit Testing

JUnit 5 and Mockito were used for fast service-layer unit tests. Oracle and Flyway are not started for these tests; repositories, EntityManager, and service clients are mocked. Real database/container integration testing is intentionally deferred to a later testing phase.

AccountServiceTest

Create account for an active customer.

Reject inactive and nonexistent customers.

Reject Customer Service unavailability.

Reject duplicate account type.

Validate account status/close lifecycle.

Retrieve account and handle account-not-found.

Result: 10 Account Service unit tests passed.

CustomerServiceTest

Create, retrieve, update, and patch customer.

Reject duplicate email conditions.

Deactivate active customer.

Reject repeated deactivation.

Handle customer-not-found.

Result: 10 core Customer Service unit tests passed.

CustomerAddressServiceTest

Add address for active customer.

Reject inactive customer and duplicate current address.

Move previous current address to history.

Retrieve history and current addresses.

Validate address ownership and not-found scenarios.

Reject lookup when the customer does not exist.

Result: 10 Customer Address Service unit tests passed.

Important test-model detail

CustomerAddressResponse exposes addressType as a String. Unit-test assertions therefore compare against "HOME" or AddressType.HOME.name(), rather than comparing the enum object directly.


